From 140d1193ed7a897d2b22b9f1c7c30a520dee2a55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 23:25:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Bound desktop driver readiness wait

load_desktop_driver() sends WM_NULL to the desktop window with an
unbounded send_message() call while waiting for the graphics driver to
be ready.

This can wedge when the caller owns the desktop window thread, since the
reply would have to be handled by the waiting thread itself. It can also
wedge when two processes enter the same driver-load path and each waits
for the other to reply.

Skip the send when the caller owns the desktop window thread, and bound
the peer wait with SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG. The send is only a readiness
barrier; timing out leaves the later property lookup to decide whether a
driver is ready.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <Alexander.Schiffhauer@gmail.com>
---
 dlls/win32u/driver.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/driver.c b/dlls/win32u/driver.c
index def6f7c..f404168 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/driver.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/driver.c
@@ -959,7 +959,11 @@ static BOOL load_desktop_driver( HWND hwnd )
 
     asciiz_to_unicode( driver_load_error, "The explorer process failed to start." );  /* default error */
     /* wait for graphics driver to be ready */
-    send_message( hwnd, WM_NULL, 0, 0 );
+    if (get_window_thread( hwnd, NULL ) == GetCurrentThreadId())
+        TRACE( "skipping desktop driver readiness wait for owned hwnd %p\n", hwnd );
+    else
+        send_message_timeout( hwnd, WM_NULL, 0, 0, SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG | SMTO_NORMAL,
+                              5000, FALSE );
 
     guid_atom = HandleToULong( NtUserGetProp( hwnd, prop_nameW ));
     memcpy( key, guid_key_prefixW, sizeof(guid_key_prefixW) );
